sequenceDiagram
  %% Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review (2026-11-06): the Gateway holds each Route-serving Node from admission to the terminal state; a second Route write on it waits (docs/reference/routes.md#coordinate-publication).
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, one Swamp run, certificate signing is the one step-to-Gateway call. docs/reference/routes.md#create-and-change-targets.
  %% Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review (2026-11-06): the site child is one Ansible phase per Node (tags site), because each placed Swamp step costs about 1.2 s and the child ran 30 in series (47.6 s measured).
  %% Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review (2026-11-06): private DNS is published beside the site install, not last (it waited 4 to 7 s for the site and the probe it does not depend on).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: route:create
  %% kind: route.create
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane V icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as Route Nodes<br/>workload · Router
  participant V as VPN Node<br/>private DNS
  CLI->>GW: route:create<br/>INSTANCE DOMAIN
  Note over GW: Validate, reserve domain<br/>Route pending
  alt identical request, Route active
    GW-->>CLI: Skipped<br/>route.exists · no run
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the command succeeds and changes nothing; a different request for the domain is refused with `route.retry_conflict`
  else new or pending Route
    Note over GW: Hold the Route Nodes
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - holds each Node that serves this Route's site (Caddy and PHP) from admission to the terminal state
    %%> - a second Route write on one of those Nodes waits (task status `waiting`) and starts when the Node is free, oldest first
    %%> Not held:
    %%> - the DNS Node: every publication writes the whole private DNS and the newest revision wins, so two publications cannot lose each other's change
    %%> Limit:
    %%> - two Route writes on one Node run one after the other, so each waits for the other's whole run
    %%> - a newer write waits behind an older waiting one that shares a Node, and a waiting write can be cancelled
    %%> - a timed-out write keeps its Nodes until Swamp confirms that its run stopped, or for 15 minutes
    %%> - task provision and cancel, instance:register and the Cluster Router writes hold the Nodes for their Route-publish step only, through the `route-hold` call
    %%> - a task that waits starts from the Node's live files; a site block that matches none of its captured states still stops it with `owned_revision_conflict`
    GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-route-create
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
    SW->>N: Make a CSR on the Node<br/>openssl req · key stays on Node
    SW->>GW: Sign the CSR<br/>operation:direct:certificate-sign
    %%> Why a call to the Gateway:
    %%> - certificate signing is the one allowed step-to-Gateway call; the Orbit CA stays in the Gateway
    GW-->>SW: Signed certificate
    opt Cluster-scoped Route
      SW->>N: Allow the Router on LAN<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/firewall
    end
    SW->>N: Install cert, publish site<br/>child route-create-site · Ansible
    %%> How:
    %%> - each PHP-FPM unit is reloaded and enabled; a stopped one starts (a task VM image keeps PHP-FPM off)
    opt domain outside the TLD
      SW->>V: Publish private DNS<br/>child dns-publish
      %%> When:
      %%> - beside the site install, not after the probe: it needs nothing from the site and waits only for the earlier steps. A failed install can leave a record that points at a Node without the site, and a failed DNS publish now skips the probe and the Ingress edge; a rerun or the Route removal replaces the record
    end
    SW->>N: Probe the site over TLS<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · SNI domain
    %%> Why:
    %%> - the probe checks the hostname and the trusted chain; it does not need a successful application HTTP response
    opt --publication=public
      SW->>N: Open the Ingress edge<br/>Ingress Caddy · ufw 80/443
    end
    alt every step succeeds
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event + outputs
      Note over GW: Record result<br/>Route active
    else a step fails
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
      Note over GW: Record the failure<br/>Route pending · failed step
      %%> On the Nodes:
      %%> - a failed validation leaves the candidate Caddyfile and stops the reload; other changes stay; there is no rollback
      %%> Retry:
      %%> - fix the cause and run the same command again; it resumes the pending Route
      %%> - `route:destroy` removes the Route and its files
    end
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
